AB  - Multimodal retrieval augmented generation improves evidence-grounded question answering by providing multimodal large language models with images, text, tables, and optical-character-recognition content. Existing pipelines commonly apply a fixed retrieval procedure despite query-level variation in evidence quality. This paper proposes CAMRAG, a confidence aware framework that combines calibrated retrieval scores, score margins, cross-modal agreement, and modality coverage. Low-confidence questions trigger one rewrite and supplementary retrieval; a cumulative-confidence rule then constructs a compact context. CAMRAG achieves 44.8 EM, 54.9 F1, and 76.5 evidence recall on WebQA, and 55.2 EM, 64.7 F1, and 81.8 evidence recall on MultiModalQA. Only 38.6% of questions trigger supplementary retrieval at the selected threshold. These results demonstrate consistent gains under the evaluated benchmarks while avoiding repeated retrieval for most queries.
