AB  - Intelligent question answering (QA) systems based on large language models (LLMs) have seen increasing application, especially with the integration of retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) techniques. These systems have proven valuable in areas such as intelligent customer service and virtual assistants. However, traditional chunking methods often fail to capture the semantic and structural relationships within documents, resulting in fragmented context. This paper proposes HRAG-QA, a novel high-precision retrieval-augmented generation approach that leverages structured document storage to enhance retrieval and response performance. Simulation-based evaluations demonstrate that HRAG-QA outperforms existing techniques in retrieval recall, mean reciprocal rank, and answer accuracy, highlighting the potential for improved QA system performance and scalability. The implementation code and datasets used in this study are available at https://github.com/Thedaizheng/rag_system.
