AB  - Bangladesh’s education system heavily relies on National Curriculum and Textbook Board (NCTB) resources, which serve as the primary knowledge base for millions of students across the country. However, digital tools for interactive learning in Bangla remain limited, particularly in supporting direct question answering from these textbooks. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances educational chatbots by improving accuracy and contextual relevance while mitigating hallucinations in large language models. Although RAG systems have been applied globally in language learning, programming, health, and legal education, no system currently addresses Bangla textbook question answering. To address this, we propose B-RAG, a RAGpowered chatbot that retrieves and generates accurate Bangla responses from NCTB content. The system indexes textbook content into a vector database, performs semantic retrieval, and generates responses via a large language model, deployed through a Streamlit interface with FastAPI. Evaluation using MultiClassification, Token-Similarity, and Token-Level F1 metrics shows high retrieval accuracy, strong linguistic alignment, and precise answer generation, demonstrating B-RAG’s potential for context-aware educational support in Bangla.
