AB  - The growth of e-commerce has led to an increasing demand for smart and scalable customer support systems. Traditional chatbots remain less effective since they are more prone to giving incorrect responses due to poor contextual understanding and brittle rule-based reasoning. This paper proposes the use of a Retrieval-Augmented-Generation based laptop assistance chatbot that effectively combines semantic search with large language models powers to provide smart, context-sensitive responses to troubleshoot laptops of top few brands . Product guides and support documents are chunked, processed, and stored in a vector database to enable real-time retrieval. Given a customer's query, the chatbot retrieves the most relevant chunks of documents and leverages a large language model to generate human-like answers. Moreover, the system supports smart recommendations of YouTube videos relevant to the user's question, which enhances guidance over troubleshooting and product usage. The proposed model was evaluated with the RAGAS metric, achieving a faithfulness of 0.81, answer relevance of 0.76, and context precision and recall of 0.74, to show strong factual grounding and contextual reliability. Overall, the system greatly improves response accuracy, reduces human-agent load, and enhances customer experience in resolving laptop related issues.
