AB  - Large language models (LLMs) have demonstrated remarkable capabilities in natural language processing tasks. However, in intelligent question-answering (QA) applications within vertical domains, they are highly prone to hallucinations due to a lack of domain-specific knowledge. Retrieval-Augmented Generation effectively mitigates this issue by integrating external knowledge bases. In this paper, we propose a RAG framework tailored for product manual QA. First, we utilize LLMs to convert illustrations within the manuals into natural language descriptions, and perform hierarchical chunking on the manual content based on Markdown heading structures to construct a knowledge base dedicated to product documents. Subsequently, a hierarchical document routing method is employed to identify the specific product manual targeted by the user's query, thereby narrowing the retrieval scope. Building upon this, a hybrid retrieval approach—combining keyword retrieval and semantic vector retrieval—is applied to extract the top-K relevant chunks. Finally, LLM generates a comprehensive response containing both textual explanations and relevant illustrations based on the retrieved results. Experimental results demonstrate that, compared to baseline methods, our proposed approach improves the final score from 0.7286 to 0.7943, validating the effectiveness of this framework in product manual QA scenarios.
ER  - 

