AB  - A methodology to develop a chatbot specialized in querying course contents is proposed in this paper. The targeted problem here is how to retrieve information from documents with mixture of different formats (text, images, equations). The proposed approach that treats each page of information as an image, divides the image into grid of patches and generates embeddings for each patch revealed to be a promising solution. Combining Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and Chain-of-Thought Augmented Generation (CAG) techniques proved effective in retrieving relevant information and generating coherent and detailed responses. The contribution of this work are the empirical tests that showed how the use of RAG significantly reduces the tendency for generic answers or hallucinations by the model, while CAG improves the structure and depth of responses, especially for complex questions.
