AB  - Cancer is one of the leading causes of death worldwide, with millions of new cases and deaths reported each year. As cancer-related research and guidelines progress at a fast pace, both patients and healthcare professionals face difficulties in accessing trustworthy and up-to-date information. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture is introduced using the LangChain framework to solve this problem by combining generative capabilities of LLM and vector-based retrieval. The knowledge used in this chatbot consists of cancer-related articles from NIH and hundreds of research abstracts related to cancer from PubMed. Users can ask the chatbot about cancer-related questions, such as symptoms, diagnosis, and treatment. The chatbot generates responses using the retrieved information from the vector database and provides the retrieved sources. RAGAS framework and 50 questions from the MedQuAD dataset are used to evaluate the chatbot’s performance in faithfulness, context precision, answer relevancy, and context recall. The retrieval showed robust performance, but the generation component still struggles. This can be further improved by using pre-trained LLMs and better prompting techniques. Future work will focus on developing better knowledge base and better chunking strategies.
ER  - 

