AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances Large Language Models (LLMs) by incorporating external knowledge. However, parametric RAG (PRAG) methods often suffer from redundancy and noise sensitivity, leading to inefficiency and degraded robustness. We propose ActiveParam, a framework for selective knowledge parameterization. ActiveParam introduces a Knowledge Probing stage, where the LLM computes an ignorance score to identify knowledge gaps for each document. Only documents with high scores, indicating novel information, are parameterized through lightweight adapters. Experiments on four question-answering benchmarks and three LLMs show that ActiveParam consistently improves F1 scores by 2-5 points over baselines like Naive Combine, while simultaneously reducing the number of required parameter adapters. This work thus establishes that selective parameterization, guided by our novel ignorance score, offers a more efficient and robust path for knowledge augmentation.
ER  - 

