AB  - We introduced a memory-augmented chatbot system to enhance the conversational capabilities of large language models (LLMs) using retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). The system enables fluid, context-aware dialogue by integrating historical interactions into the reasoning process. Through a configurable memory setting, the chatbot tracks prior user queries and responses, allowing it to resolve ambiguous or underspecified inputs with greater accuracy. The RAG architecture enables the chatbot's outputs in both dynamic conversation history and external knowledge sources, allowing the model to produce more relevant and coherent responses. Built on FastAPI and integrated with LangChain and OpenAI's GPT-4o-mini, the system captures and reuses conversation context across turns, delivering a natural and human-like chat experience. The design demonstrates how the combination of memory retention and real-time retrieval empowers LLMs to perform more intelligently in open-ended, multi-turn interactions.
