AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) technology serves as an external knowledge integration mechanism for large language models, addressing the bottlenecks of traditional AI in knowledge timeliness and expertise through the organic fusion of language understanding, knowledge retrieval, and logical generation. RAG systems follow a three-stage closed loop of “knowledge construction-positioning-generation,” first transforming business documents into vector representations through structured preprocessing to establish a searchable knowledge foundation, then precisely locating knowledge fragments highly relevant to user questions based on semantic similarity retrieval and multi-dimensional reranking mechanisms, and finally generating accurate and traceable professional responses through large language models combined with retrieved content. In the practice of power grid control domain, the team conducted systematic work around the construction of control business knowledge bases and intelligent question-answering capability development, constructing structured control knowledge bases for core regulatory documents such as the “Power Grid Stability Regulations” through semantic segmentation, clause extraction, table restoration and other technologies, and establishing question-answering systems with multi-turn interaction and professional adaptability based on vector retrieval frameworks and large language models, achieving a capability transition from “regulatory documents” to “intelligent knowledge services.” Facing the professional challenges of the power sector, the team achieved breakthroughs in three core technical directions: adopting hierarchical segmentation strategies, semantic inheritance mechanisms, and metadata enhancement technologies to solve the semantic fragmentation problems caused by traditional slicing methods; overcoming the parsing challenges of structured tables in power documents based on improved layout recognition and structure recognition algorithms; and significantly improving the semantic representation accuracy of professional terminology through deep adaptive training of general Embedding models with power professional corpora.
