AB  - Electricity trading rule interpretation requires accurate answers grounded in regulatory documents. However, direct use of large language models often leads to hallucination, while standard retrieval-augmented generation may introduce redundant context and excessive token cost. To address these issues, this paper proposes a token-aware retrieval-augmented framework that combines hybrid retrieval, reranking, and context selection. Experiments on four task types show that the proposed method improves accuracy, evidence grounding, and token efficiency over direct QA and standard RAG. The results indicate that effective context organization is essential for reliable and efficient rule interpretation.
