AB  - The growth of multimedia content and user interactions has created a pressing need for intelligent, scalable conversational agents capable of providing personalized, context-aware responses. In this paper, we propose a novel framework that integrates retrieval-augmented generation with recommendation techniques to develop scalable movie chatbots. Our approach leverages large-scale knowledge graphs to capture rich semantic relationships among movies and user pReferences. At the same time, the retrieval-augmented generation mechanism enhances response quality by dynamically incorporating relevant external knowledge. We design an efficient graph learning model that scales with increasing data size and supports real-time chatbot interactions. Experimental evaluations show that supplementing the system with historical information from the recommendation module produces more personalized suggestions than either standalone module. This architecture combines big data-driven graph analytics with generative language models, offering a robust solution for movie chatbots.
