AB  - This work proposes a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)-based medical question-answering chatbot designed for resource-constrained platforms. The proposed Medical Retrieval & Summarization (MRS) module integrates dense passage retrieval for semantically rich search, PEGASUS for summarizing retrieved content, and a refinement module called Gateformer to enhance summary-question alignment. This design reduces redundancy and emphasizes key information, enabling LLAMA-3 8B to produce high-quality answers without fine-tuning. Experiments on PubMedQA demonstrate that the proposed approach achieves 74.00% accuracy, outperforming BM25 + prompt-based LLM and narrowing the gap between small and large-scale Large Language Models (LLMs). These results highlight the effectiveness of our MRS in optimizing retrieval and summarization, enhancing small LLMs for specific applications.
