AB  - The Healthcare Chatbot with Medical Document Retrieval actually makes sense of those dense medical documents that people struggle with—lab reports, prescriptions, all that stuff. You start by uploading your documents to the system and it automatically extracts the relevant information with a technique called Corrective Retrieval Augmented Generation or Corrective RAG. Then it gets a large language model from Google Gemini, for instance, to interpret and rephrase the resulting information in simple English. The most amazing thing is, besides this function, there is a fact checker which verifies the chatbot's responses against the actual knowledge in your files. Thus, you receive reliable clarifications, not mere conjectures. The chatbot assesses clinical measurements, offers patient-friendly summaries, explains medical jargon, and facilitates interactive questionanswering. The solution improves reliability and usability in medical AI applications by combining multimodal document processing, vector-based retrieval, and corrective self-verification. Its privacy-first architecture guaranties the safe management of private health information while providing prompt, relevant, and transparent solutions. This study shows how contemporary LLMs can be combined with retrieval and validation methods to create healthcare assistants that are safe, effective, and user-centered.
