AB  - The defense industry is characterized by a rapid proliferation of complex technical documentation, predominantly stored in unstructured formats such as PDF brochures and datasheets. Extracting precise, context-aware information from these documents remains a significant challenge for traditional keyword-based search engines. This study proposes a domain-specific Question Answering (QA) system that utilizes RetrievalAugmented Generation (RAG) to address this gap in the context of the Turkish Defense Industry. By integrating dense vector embeddings (MPNet) with a vector similarity search (FAISS) and a Large Language Model (LLM), we construct a semantic knowledge base from official product brochures. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed RAG architecture significantly outperforms traditional Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency (TF-IDF) baselines, achieving ROUGE-1 and Semantic Similarity scores of 0.677 and 0.605, respectively. These findings validate the efficacy of semantic search in handling the specific terminological nuances of defense industry literature.
