AB  - Electric power safety question answering demands both precision and domain expertise, yet existing systems often rely on unstructured documents that are difficult to maintain and prone to retrieval inconsistencies. We present EPSQA, a domain-specific Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework that uniquely leverages structured electric power safety question banks curated by experts. EPSQA incorporates large language model–based keyword extraction and SQL-driven database retrieval to align query intent with relevant domain knowledge. By introducing adaptive matching strategies, EPSQA enables fine-grained control over retrieval precision and coverage. Evaluated on a real-world electric power safety dataset, EPSQA achieves a correct answer rate of approximately 57.44%, representing a relative improvement of about 72% over the unstructured baseline.
