AB  - Rice, also called Oryza sativa, is important worldwide as a food crop, but Brunei Darussalam has difficulty producing enough rice and relies heavily on imports to feed its people. Due to limited resources, an older workforce, and a lack of workers, we urgently need to improve crop production. These problems are worsened by diseases and pests that can significantly affect the quality and yield of rice crops. At the same time, old ways of diagnosing these issues are unreliable and time-consuming. This project aims to create an AI-powered robot for farmers that uses smart technologies to quickly identify diseases and pests affecting rice plants. The chatbot provides quick, accurate diagnoses and personalized management advice to improve resource use, reduce labour issues, and boost the sustainability and efficiency of rice farming in Brunei.
