AB  - The quality of retrieved context is a critical bottleneck for Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems, as existing refinement methods often provide noisy or irrelevant information. Current approaches are typically limited to single-metric, document-level filtering or risk degrading the generator’s capabilities through coupled end-to-end fine-tuning. To address this, we introduce ProRank, a progressive two-stage pipeline that uses a fine-tuned, multidimensional LLM reranker for document-level selection, followed by fine-grained intra-document refinement to construct a highly information-dense context. This decoupled approach preserves the generator’s integrity while achieving state-of-the-art performance on knowledge-intensive benchmarks.
ER  - 

