AB  - Accessing information from unstructured government documents remains challenging due to the limitations of keyword-based retrieval and the hallucination issues of Large Language Models (LLMs). This study proposes a structure-aware Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework for question answering over Indonesian governmental regulations by integrating query expansion, pasal-boundary-aware chunking, and adaptive context expansion. The framework is evaluated using three LLMs—LLaMA-3.1 8B, DeepSeek R1 8B, and Qwen3 8B—on 100s question-answer pairs using Accuracy, ROUGE-L, BLEU, and Jaccard Similarity. Experimental results show that LLaMA-3.1 8B and Qwen3 8B achieved the highest accuracy of 90.00%, while DeepSeek R1 8B obtained 89.00%. LLaMA-3.1 8B also achieved the highest ROUGE-L F1 (0.8607), BLEU (0.7394), and Jaccard Similarity (0.7610), indicating stronger fidelity to the source documents. These results demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed framework for question answering over Indonesian governmental regulations while highlighting the trade-off between factual accuracy and textual fidelity across different LLMs.
