AB  - Dementia, a neurocognitive disorder, is projected to increase to 139 million cases by 2050 worldwide. To handle this, a non-invasive non-optical scaling screening is needed. The study proposed the use of the Advanced Hybrid Cognitive Assessment Framework (AHCAF), a framework using Large Language Models (LLMs) as a base along with Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) to implement the initial step towards neurocognitive assessment. In this study, a clinical examination system with interactive dialogues was developed. AHCAF system aims to detect early-stage cognitive impairment of $87 \%$ and $85 \%$ accuracy and sensitivity, respectively, in 500 patients. The baseline of the experimental performance shows that the framework is much more effective than the Mini-Mental state examination (MMSE), and approximately 84% and 90% in the intent routing process and in the generation of the diagnostic report, respectively.
