AB  - This paper designs and implements an enterprise-level intelligent question-answering (Q&A) system based on the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture. The system comprehensively utilizes prompt engineering, the LangChain framework, the ChatGLM large language model, and the FAISS vector database, all deployed in a localized environment. It aims to address the needs for enterprise data privacy and precise Q&A on domain-specific knowledge. The system implements a hot-loading mechanism for prompt templates and supports dynamic management of knowledge bases in various formats such as PDF and DOCX. Test results indicate that the system achieves a maximum accuracy of 85% in Q&A tasks, with an average response time of less than 1 second. This effectively verifies that the system can provide enterprises with efficient and accurate knowledge services while ensuring data security.
