AB  - In the rapidly evolving landscape of higher education, institutions are constantly seeking innovative digital solutions to streamline administrative processes and enhance student engagement. Prospective and current students often encounter significant friction when attempting to access timely and accurate information regarding admissions, curriculum details, fee structures, and campus facilities. Traditional enquiry methods, such as manual help desks and static web portals, frequently suffer from limited availability, information latency, and human error. To address these critical challenges, this paper presents the design, implementation, and comprehensive evaluation of a "Smart Educational College Chatbot," specifically tailored for Sri Jagadguru Chandrashekaranatha Swamiji Institute of Technology (SJCIT). The proposed system utilizes a novel hybrid architecture that synergizes rule-based local logic with the advanced generative capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs), specifically integrating Google’s Gemini 1.5 Flash. To ensure high fidelity and domain specificity, the chatbot employs a robust Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework, grounding its responses in a verifiable institutional knowledge base. Furthermore, the system features novel utility-enhancing modules such as "Document Droid" for automated certificate generation and a "Grade Calculator," alongside comprehensive voice-to-text accessibility features. Experimental results indicate that the chatbot significantly reduces administrative workload and improves information retrieval efficiency by over 40% compared to traditional manual methods.
