Y1  - 20-22 May 2026
AB  - Documentation in real-time is time consuming and a tiring process to do manually. To overcome this, documentation process can be automated using LLMs. Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) has become one of the most important techniques for improving the accuracy of Large Language Models by combining knowledge from external sources. However, many RAG systems are not multi-user friendly and depends on cloud-based systems which reduces the scalability and data privacy. This paper provides the design and implementation of a multi-user RAG chatbot system which is useful in deriving insights from documents without any hallucination and provides only the necessary content to be provided for the given query or question. The proposed system supports indexing of documents per user with having the conversations being stored using a vector storage called ChromaDB which helps in the reuse of the previously indexed document while maintaining data separation across multiple users by using a LangChain framework and Ollama LLM. This architecture supports PDF ingestion, recursively chunks the text data, dense vector embeddings by using nomic-embed-text, similarity-based retrieval using a vector database and generates conversational response by hosting a Mistral LLM. The system has user management and session management as it enables the user to have their login credentials. The system also enables saving of the chat history with customised chat history name, deletion of the indexed documents and clearing of the conversations with the chatbot. The system also provides an expandable chat history. The evaluation of the proposed system shows that the model achieves low response latency once the document being indexed. This chatbot is not dependent on any other external APIs and uses Streamlit. Thus, the proposed paper provides a cost-efficient RAG system by using a LLM called Mistral from Ollama.
